{
  "area": "mechanic-fishing",
  "description": "Fishing (packages/core/docs/native-production.md §3.3): whether this water may be fished, what it holds, and how much of it is left. Each kb mirrors FISHING_PREDICATES_PROLOG verbatim and is regenerated by `npm run production-corpus`. What this pack answers is what the water HOLDS; what came up on THIS cast is a seeded draw core owns. spot_stock/2 is the whole of what v1 was missing under its roll — a pool that never ran down is a vending machine — and a weight-0 fishery_catch/3 row is how a world says the salmon stopped running without deleting the row a quest still reads. Every number is whole and there is no percentage anywhere in the pack — a weight is a relative integer, never a probability — and, unlike the v1 mechanic this replaces, there is NO ROLL IN THE PACK AT ALL: v1 drew Math.random() against a hardcoded content table in four separate engine classes, which no native engine can reproduce. What a seeded draw turns up is core’s and is pinned by conformance/production/draws.json instead, because a hash is not expressible as a rule (packages/core/docs/native-production.md §6, divergence P-1). What is NOT here is an item: every output atom is one conformance/prolog/mechanic-equipment.json already owns, and a second item taxonomy here would be the parallel one these four modules exist not to be. Neither is the gate on the work itself — whether a person MAY dig this seam is one more clause of forbids/4, permissible/3 belongs to conformance/prolog/agent-ai.json, and that a refused job writes nothing at all is proved end to end in packages/core/src/game-engine/logic/__tests__/ProductionDirector.test.ts.",
